## E3 — tail-latency percentiles (chase, 4G region, 2M samples, ns)
# config            mean   p50  p90  p99  p99.9  p99.99  max
cxl-idle            291.4  279  299  559  679    3449    84009
cxl-load4T          351.6  320  460  690  840    2950    150650
cxl-load12T         345.5  319  419  689  799    2359    21749
dram-idle           178.8  169  229  329  439    1769    17539
dram-load12T        179.7  169  229  329  429    1969    17319
# Findings: (1) No Melody-style microsecond p99.9 tails on CZ120 Pair A — p99.9
# stays sub-us at all loads. (2) p99.99+ spikes appear on BOTH nodes (system/
# interrupt noise dominates the extreme tail; CXL's are ~2x DRAM's). (3) Real
# load asymmetry: CXL median inflates +15% under own 12T load (279->319ns) and
# p90 +40-54%; DRAM is completely flat under the same load. (4) Tail-aware
# routing (Idea 4 signal) looks WEAK on this hardware at these loads.

